        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "App Settings Panel & Mouse Sensitivity",
        "subtitle": "No user-facing control for mouse/zoom sensitivity exists, and there is no App Settings surface at all — app-level preferences are scattered across three uncoordinated mechanisms, mostly surfaced inside the wrong dialog.",
        "intent": "headline",
        "status": "active",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/template-structure/title.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-goal",
      "type": "goal",
      "label": "Goal",
      "position": {
        "x": -1120,
        "y": -520
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Give the app a real App Settings surface, distinct from per-graph Document Settings, and make mouse/zoom sensitivity a real setting on it",
        "body": "Triggered by: after the workspace-zoom-jank fix landed, zoom felt \"obnoxiously sluggish\" — there is no way for a user to adjust that, which surfaced a bigger gap.\n\nCONFIRMED, three overlapping places a \"setting\" can live today, and none of them is a proper App Settings panel:\n\n1. Per-graph settings — live on a Declaration node's own data.settings (layout, autoSave, theme, backgroundImage, defaultNodeColor, defaultEdgeColor, snapToGrid, gridSize, edgeRouting, github). Correctly scoped, not part of this problem.\n\n2. components/GraphEditor/settingsManager.js — a REAL, already-existing app-level store (localStorage key 'nodegraph-editor-settings'), holding theme, watermark, default colors, panel anchors, shortcuts. But only watermarkEnabled/watermarkStrength/showFocusIndicator are actually wired to any UI, and that UI lives inside components/GraphEditor/components/DocumentPropertiesDialog.js's \"Appearance\" tab — presented as if it were a per-document setting even though the underlying store is global. saveSettings() also silently no-ops when localStorage.getItem('isFreeUser') === 'true' — undecided whether that's intentional gating or a forgotten guard; a free-tier user can change these controls and have nothing persist, with no error shown.\n\n3. Standalone, uncoordinated localStorage keys — 'twilite.uiDensity' is set directly from DocumentPropertiesDialog.js:429 (and read in Browser.js, GraphEditorContent.js, DynamicViewNode.js), completely bypassing settingsManager.js. A second global-preference mechanism doing the same job as #2, not unified with it.\n\nMOUSE SENSITIVITY, specifically — there is no setting because there is no variable:\ncomponents/NodeGraph/PanZoomLayer.js:349 and :369 both hardcode `const zoomSpeed = 0.002;` — the same magic number, duplicated in the throttled-tick path and the trailing-debounce path. No UI anywhere reads or writes it. (Likely explanation for \"the fix worked but now it's sluggish\": before the render-churn fix, the wheel listener tearing down/reinstalling every render was probably applying zoom more than once per gesture, accidentally amplifying apparent sensitivity. Now it applies cleanly once per tick, so the bare 0.002 is what's actually being felt for the first time. This needed to be a setting regardless of that fix.)",
        "status": "open",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A real App Settings panel exists, separate from the Document Properties dialog",
          "Mouse/zoom sensitivity is a real, persisted, user-adjustable setting, replacing the hardcoded duplicated zoomSpeed constant",
          "watermarkEnabled/watermarkStrength/showFocusIndicator/uiDensity are controlled from the new App Settings panel, not Document Properties",
          "All app-level settings go through one unified store (settingsManager.js), not a mix of it and standalone localStorage keys",
          "Document Properties retains only genuinely per-graph settings (GitHub binding, edge layout, graph theme-node authority, overview/activity)"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-1",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1600,
        "y": -80
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Build the App Settings panel surface",
        "body": "A new panel/dialog, reachable independently of any open graph (unlike Document Properties, which only makes sense with a graph open). Backed by components/GraphEditor/settingsManager.js's existing loadSettings/saveSettings/resetSettings — clean up that module's stale bits (the unused introGraph stub, the \"NodeGraph Editor\" naming) rather than building a second store beside it. Where exactly it's reached from (browser chrome, a menu item, a keyboard shortcut) is a UI placement decision — make a reasonable call, it's not the hard part of this task.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A new App Settings panel component exists and is reachable from the UI without a graph open",
          "It reads from and writes to settingsManager.js, not a new parallel store",
          "settingsManager.js’s dead/stale content (introGraph stub, old product-name references) is cleaned up while it’s open, not left for later"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-2",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1120,
        "y": -80
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Add mouse/zoom sensitivity as a real setting",
        "body": "Replace the hardcoded, duplicated `const zoomSpeed = 0.002;` at PanZoomLayer.js:349 and :369 with a single shared value sourced from the new App Settings store, with 0.002 as the default so existing behavior doesn't change until a user adjusts it. Check other zoom-input paths (keyboard zoom keys, pinch/touch if present) for their own hardcoded step values and decide whether they should scale with the same sensitivity setting for consistency, or intentionally stay independent — that's this task's open question, not an assumption to make silently.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "zoomSpeed is no longer duplicated as a hardcoded literal in two places",
          "A user-adjustable sensitivity setting exists in App Settings and actually changes wheel-zoom responsiveness",
          "Default behavior (0.002-equivalent) is unchanged for a user who never touches the new setting",
          "Other zoom-input paths (keyboard, touch/pinch) are at least audited for the same hardcoded-constant pattern, even if the decision is to leave them independent"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-3",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1600,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Migrate uiDensity into the unified settings store",
        "body": "'twilite.uiDensity' is currently its own standalone localStorage key, set directly from DocumentPropertiesDialog.js:429 and read independently in Browser.js, GraphEditorContent.js, and DynamicViewNode.js (two places). Move it into settingsManager.js's store so there's one app-level settings mechanism, not two. Update all four read sites and the one write site. Verify uiDensity still applies correctly everywhere it currently does after the move — this is a real behavior-preserving migration, not just a relocation.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "uiDensity is read from and written to settingsManager.js’s store, not a standalone localStorage key",
          "All existing read sites (Browser.js, GraphEditorContent.js, DynamicViewNode.js x2) are updated",
          "Interface density still visibly changes correctly after the migration, verified live"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-4",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1120,
        "y": 400
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Move watermark/focus-indicator controls out of Document Properties",
        "body": "watermarkEnabled, watermarkStrength, and showFocusIndicator are currently edited from DocumentPropertiesDialog.js's \"Appearance\" tab (around lines 1047-1111) even though they already read/write the global settingsManager.js store, not anything document-scoped. Move their UI into the new App Settings panel. Leave Document Properties' Appearance tab with only what's genuinely per-graph there (the Graph Theme Node section, Canvas & Background's graph-surface-specific parts if any survive review).",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "watermarkEnabled/watermarkStrength/showFocusIndicator controls appear in App Settings, not Document Properties",
          "They still take effect the same way (eventBus emits updateEditorWatermark/updateEditorFocusIndicator unchanged) after the move",
          "Document Properties’ Appearance tab no longer contains settings that aren’t actually about this specific graph"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-5",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1600,
        "y": 880
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Resolve the isFreeUser silent no-op in saveSettings()",
        "body": "settingsManager.js's saveSettings() currently does nothing — no error, no toast, no visible feedback — when localStorage.getItem('isFreeUser') === 'true'. Decide: is restricting app-settings persistence to paid users an intentional product decision, or a stale/forgotten guard from an earlier gating scheme? If intentional, the new App Settings panel needs to actually tell a free-tier user why their change didn't stick, instead of silently discarding it. If not intentional, remove the guard.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The isFreeUser gate’s intent is explicitly decided, not left ambiguous",
          "If kept: a free-tier user gets visible feedback when a setting change won’t persist",
          "If removed: settings persist for all users and the guard is deleted, not just bypassed"
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "asp-task-6",
      "type": "task",
      "label": "Task",
      "position": {
        "x": -1120,
        "y": 880
      },
      "width": 340,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
